  "The English teen edition quotes the ASV. Every epigraph and every direct Scripture quotation marked `mined` is Louis Segond (1910) verbatim, with only French typographic spacing before : ; ? ! added; partial quotations keep whole Segond words (e.g. Isaiah 40:31 drops Segond's opening « Mais », 1 Peter 2:23 drops the verse-final semicolon). The “(ASV)” labels were dropped and citations use French book names.",
  "Numbering shifts: Psalm 13:1 (English) is « Psaume 13:2 » in Segond; Mark 3:14's “that they might be with him, and that he might send them forth to preach” runs across Segond 3:14-15, so the ch. 8 epigraph cites « Marc 3:14-15 » (the reference rows keep the English “Mark 3:14”). Ezekiel 3:17 in Segond says « sentinelle », not « veilleur »; the body keeps « veilleur » for Nee's name, as the full French biography does.",
  "Names, terms and titles follow the French Portraits de courage biography (watchman-nee-a-life.fr): crécelle du veilleur de nuit, Ni Shuzu / Ni Tuosheng, Lin Heping, Dora Yu, Charity Chang, Margaret E. Barber, Petit Troupeau, Assembly Hall, Frères exclusifs, Mouvement patriotique des trois autonomies, rééducation par le travail, brisement de l’homme extérieur, savoir / compter / présenter; book titles La vie chrétienne normale, L’homme spirituel, Assis, marchez, tenez ferme; George Müller with the umlaut. Teen voice uses « tu » and passé simple narration as in a-retrospect-teens.fr; title « Watchman Nee (Pour ados) » (25 chars).",
  "Self-rendered echoes needing a native check: Matthew 10:23 (fleeing from city to city, ch. 10), « Jusques à quand ? » (ch. 11, Segond words but not Segond punctuation) and « le trésor dans des vases d’argile » (ch. 13). Romans 6:11's “reckon” is Segond « regardez-vous », while the teaching keyword stays « compter » as in the biography. AI-translated in-session; awaiting native review."
